verses.text:
Awake, awake, Deborah;
Awake, awake, utter a song;
Rise, Barak, and take captive thy captivity,
Son of Abinoam.

Kings came—they fought;
Then fought kings of Canaan,
In Taanach, by the waters of Megiddo;
Gain of money they took not!

Between her feet he bowed—
He fell, he lay down;
Between her feet he bowed, he fell;
Where he bowed, there he fell—destroyed.
